---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { line } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const hogs = assertion('the-hogs-multiplied-as-the-keepers-halved')

const hogSpec = line(
  hogs.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  [{ name: 'Hogs on 31 December', y: hogs.figures.map((f) => f.value) }],
  { yTitle: 'Head', labelLast: true, zeroBased: true },
)
---

<Article slug="a-hog-county">
  <p>
    The county profile the census publishes for a general reader leads with farms, land and sales,
    and all three of them barely move. The figure that moved is an inventory row on the second
    page.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={hogs} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="hogs"
    title="Hogs in Allen County, 2002–2022"
    caption="Inventory at 31 December of each census year. The operations holding them went 59, 60, 46, 56, 28 across the same five censuses."
    columns={['Census', 'Head']}
    rows={hogs.figures.map((f) => [f.label, f.value.toLocaleString('en-US')])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="hogs" set:html={JSON.stringify(hogSpec)} is:inline />
  <p>
    Hogs are $75.3 million of the county's $240.8 million of agricultural sales, which is fourth
    in Ohio. Of 377,816 head sold in 2022, 281,194 were raised under production contract on twelve
    operations — the census's own term for an animal fed by one party and owned by another. In
    2017 it was 144,480 of 324,947 on twenty-one. The share went from 44 per cent to 74 while the
    number of places doing it fell by nine.
  </p>
  <p>
    In 1910 this county held 59,695 swine and 56,580 people, and the measure written from that
    census observed that the swine outnumbered the people. They still do, by 235,800 to 100,866.
    Everything else in the 1910 count is gone: 14,676 horses became 316, 41,240 sheep and goats
    became 1,499, and the 10,671 dairy cows became a figure the census will not print, because
    eight operations hold it and one is large enough that the total would disclose it.
  </p>
</Article>
